From: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:54:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Fix ESP32 interrupt routing and clock ticks

Install chip-specific interrupt matrices, CLIC/PLIC state and CPU gates.
Keep Wi-Fi/Bluetooth routes, dedicated SMP IPIs and the emulator fallback
together with the corrected systimer frequency and boot-CPU tick policy.

Consolidates legacy kernel patches: 0002, 0009, 0012, 0013, 0014, 0015,
0016, 0017, 0019, 0021, 0032, 0034, 0035, 0036, 0037, 0038, 0039.

Co-authored-by: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
